1 NAME Anders Gustaf /Linder/
2 GIVN Anders Gustaf
2 SURN Linder
2 _MARNM Linder
2 NICK Anders Gustav Andersson Linder
2 NICK Anders Gustaf Linder
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 12 MAR 1803
2 PLAC Rusele
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lycksele
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE 30 JAN 1877
2 PLAC Sandsjön 
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sorsele fs
3 CTRY Sweden
1 BURI
2 DATE 3 FEB 1877
2 PLAC Sorsele, Västerbotten, Sverige
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Hemmansägare
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Linder, Anders Gustaf
2 CONT Bonde
2 CONT
2 CONT Sandsjön
2 CONT
2 CONT Död 30/1 1877.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kyrkobokförd i Sorsele (Västerbottens län, Lappland).
2 CONT
2 CONT Född 12/3 1803 i Lycksele (Västerbottens län, Lappland).
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift man (30/3 1861).
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Gustaf Linder (1803-1877) was the first son of the gunner Anders Johansson Linder and the ninth child of his wife the widow Anna Ulrika Lycksell. Anders Gustaf was born in Rusele. After his father came home from the war (18
2 CONC 08-1809) the whole family moved from Rusele to Sandsjön where his father had bought two homesteads. Anders Gustaf was first married to Lovisa Elisabeth Andersdotter (1807-1845) and had ten children. His first wife died in childbir
2 CONC th. He then married Christina Elisabeth (Stina-Lisa) Fredriksdotter (1822-1859) and the family had five children. Stina-Lisa died in 1859 in tuberculosis. Anders remarried a third time with the maid Anna Elisabeth “Lisa” Andersdot
2 CONC ter (1824-1898) and had four more children. When he died in 1877 he seems to be wealthy. According to the estate inventory he owned three homesteads (farms with forests) and a lot of inventories. All his children seemed to have do
2 CONC ne well. In this context that means that all but two of his male children became homestead owners (i.e. owing land and forest). Similarly, all but one of his daughters married owners of homesteads. But hard times were coming. At t
2 CONC he end of the century grain prices and price of saw timber took a turn. Further the division of farms at end of 1880s-onwards led to diminished livelihood opportunities. Some of Anders Gustaf Linder’s grandchildren therefore emigr
2 CONC ated to USA and Canada 1910-onwards. Today his descendants can be found all over the word in different professional capacities (as teachers, nurses, civil engineers, researchers, civil servants, governmental officials, consultants
2 CONC , manual workers etc.). The three homesteads in Sandsjön are still in the descendant’s possession. By Barbro Fransson
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
